# Railway dual deploy (AriForce-style)

Both **api** and **web** must auto-deploy on **every** push/merge to `main`, whether the diff touched api, web, or neither-app files.

## Required config

| Service | Branch | watchPatterns |
|---|---|---|
| api (`9fca6685-…`) | `main` | `**` (or equivalent: never skip) |
| web (`84d8a1bc-…`) | `main` | `**` (or equivalent: never skip) |

Project: `hopeful-surprise` / `0d203832-0797-41b6-ac8f-e44466d80bc2`, env production `fdb0c2b2-…`.

- Do **not** point either service at feature branches for production.
- Do **not** use narrow watchPatterns (`apps/api/**`, `apps/web/**`, etc.) that skip the other service.
- After retargeting or config changes, avoid double `connect-service-source` / redeploy storms; one trigger per service is enough (Railway queues extra deploys **within** a service).

## After merges that move the web root

When Next lives under `apps/web`, web build/start must use `@firstround/web` (not root `next`). Keep branch + watchPatterns as above.

## Agent duty

If you find api/web off `main` or with path-filtered watches, fix them back to this rule and tell Prajesh.
